body:
Yeah, I just copied over this part from whoever implemented it before me. Looking into it though, it seems that the `StringName` equality operator checks the pointer itself, while `is_empty()` checks the length of the string. I looked a bit and saw this is being used all over the engine, and the comment in the equality operator says this:

```
_FORCE_INLINE_ bool operator==(const StringName &p_name) const {
		// The real magic of all this mess happens here.
		// This is why path comparisons are very fast.
		return _data == p_name._data;
	}
```

So I figure this is preferred.

